1. Added all the necessary providers that were present in the component stack:
   - SessionProvider
   - I18nextProvider
   - QueryClientProvider
   - TooltipProvider
   - FeatureProvider

2. Added Suspense wrapper with a loading fallback for handling dynamic imports

3. Added an ErrorBoundary component to catch and display any rendering errors

4. Added proper TypeScript types for the ErrorBoundary component

5. Created a QueryClient instance with some sensible defaults

The providers are added in the same order as they appear in the component stack trace to maintain the proper context hierarchy. The ErrorBoundary will help catch and display any other errors that might occur during rendering.

Note: You might need to adjust the i18n configuration passed to I18nextProvider based on your actual i18n setup. For now, I've passed an empty object as a placeholder. If you see i18n-related errors, you'll need to provide the proper i18n instance.

